# The Baron's watch (docs/voice/vallaki_guard.md): the east gate on arrival (start), the gate afterwards (guard),
# the lockup by the stockade (jailer) and the watchman in the mansion foyer (mansion_guard).

~ start
# Ireena and Ismark travel with the party from the Village of Barovia (ireena_in_party, ismark_joins_escort).
# If the road did not already add them as guests, they join here, at the gate they set out for.
if flag.ireena_in_party and not guest:ireena
join ireena
endif
if flag.ismark_joins_escort and flag.ireena_in_party and not guest:ismark
join ismark
endif
cutscene vallaki_palisade
Narrator: The road ends at a palisade of sharpened logs twice a man's height. Most of the points face outward. A few, you notice, face in. Two watchmen with festival ribbons on their spears step into the gateway.
Town Guard: Halt. Names, business, and how long you mean to stay. And smile, please. It's the law this week.
if night
Town Guard: Gate shuts at dusk, by rights. But the Baron says travellers are good for morale, and you'd be very bad for it lying dead in the road.
endif
* We're travellers. We want a roof and a hot meal. -> honest
* [if guest:ireena] This is Ireena Kolyana, daughter of the late burgomaster of Barovia. -> ireena
* [Deception DC 12] We've come for the festival, naturally. -> festival_ok | festival_fail
* [Intimidation DC 14] We're coming in. Stand aside. -> bully_ok | bully_fail

~ honest
Town Guard: Roof and meal: the Blue Water Inn, south of the square. Ask for Urwin; don't ask him anything else. Avoid the coffin maker's. He's jumpy lately, and so's his door.
approve godrick_pendlebrook +1 kip_smudgewick +1: You told the gate the plain truth
-> rules

~ ireena
set vallaki_ireena_announced
Town Guard [afraid]: Kolyan's girl? From the village? We heard he'd died. Sorry, miss. The Baron will want to know you're here. He likes visiting dignitaries; they make a crowd look bigger.
Ireena: I'm not visiting. I'm hiding. Tell him that, if you have to tell him anything.
if guest:ismark
Ismark: And I'm her brother, before anyone in this town gets ideas.
endif
-> rules

~ festival_ok
Town Guard [smile]: For the festival! You hear that, Pyotr? They came for the festival. On purpose. Write that down; the Baron will want it for the speech.
approve wren_featherfoot +1: You talked your way through Vallaki's gate
-> rules

~ festival_fail
Town Guard: Nobody comes for the festival. Nobody comes here for anything, these days. Some weeks I'm not sure the Baron comes for the festival. Don't tell him I said that.
-> rules

~ bully_ok
Town Guard: Fine. Fine! In you go. But you'll smile when the Baron passes, or it's the stocks, and then I have to stand there watching you all day.
approve godrick_pendlebrook -1 kip_smudgewick -1 thistle +1: You shoved your way through Vallaki's gate
-> rules

~ bully_fail
set vallaki_watch_wary
Town Guard: I've eleven more like me on that wall and a Baron who enjoys a punishment more than a festival. Let's both be cheerful about this, shall we?
Narrator: The other watchman takes a stub of chalk from his pocket and writes something on the gatepost, looking at each of your faces as he does it.
interject tag:blunt: He's right. Twelve spears. Bad odds for a doorway.
-> rules

~ rules
set vallaki_arrived
quest festival_of_the_blazing_sun announced
if guest:ireena
quest sanctuary_for_ireena arrived
# The road west is behind her: the escort is over (Sanctuary for Ireena goes on from here).
if quest.escort_ireena
quest escort_ireena arrived
endif
endif
Town Guard: The rules, quick. The Festival of the Blazing Sun is in the square; the Baron lights the sun at noon and everyone attends. Lamps out at the second bell. Nobody frowns at the Baron.
Town Guard: If you've a grievance, keep it indoors. If you've a dead relative, Father Lucian at St. Andral's. If you've a live one who frowns, keep them indoors as well.
if name:godrick_pendlebrook
interject name:godrick_pendlebrook: Smiling! I can do that. Look. I'm very good at it.
else
interject tag:cheerful: I can smile. I'm smiling now. Look.
endif
if name:thistle
interject name:thistle: A law. About faces. Why?
else
interject tag:blunt: Laws about faces. Of course there are.
endif
Town Guard: Lovely. Hold it like that until you're out of sight. All will be well.
-> END

~ guard
if flag.vallaki_watch_wary and not flag.festival_over
Town Guard: Oh, it's you. "Stand aside." Pyotr drew your faces on the gatepost. Smiling, mind. It's the law.
endif
if flag.vallaki_backed == "baron"
Town Guard [smile]: Marshals! The Baron says you're to be saluted. Consider yourselves saluted. All is well. It's official now; there was a proclamation.
elif flag.vallaki_backed == "wachter"
Town Guard: New ribbons. Black ones. Lady Wachter's orders. Nobody has to smile any more. Funny thing is, nobody does.
elif flag.vallaki_backed == "neither"
Town Guard: The council says I can stop smiling at people. I keep doing it anyway. Habit. Father Lucian says that's allowed.
elif flag.festival_begun
Town Guard: Shouldn't you be in the square? Everyone's in the square. I'm in the square in spirit, and also in a lot of trouble if the sergeant counts.
elif night
Town Guard: Gate's shut. If you're going out, I didn't see you. If you're coming back, knock twice and say something cheerful.
else
Town Guard: Still here? Good. The Baron counts heads at the festival. More heads, better festival.
endif
* Heard anything interesting? -> news
* Who should we know in Vallaki? -> whos_who
* Goodbye. -> END

~ news
if flag.festival_over
Town Guard: News? You are the news. Has been for days.
-> END
endif
if not flag.bones_returned
Town Guard: Something's wrong up at St. Andral's. Father Lucian stripped the altar cloth two days back and hasn't put it back. Priests don't do that for nothing.
if not quest.bones_of_st_andral
quest bones_of_st_andral rumored
endif
endif
if not flag.arabelle_rescued and not flag.arabelle_lost
Town Guard: The Vistani outside the west gate are in an uproar. The headman's little girl's gone missing. Their brother Arrigal says she wandered. Arrigal says a lot of things.
if not quest.missing_arabelle
quest missing_arabelle rumored
endif
endif
if not flag.wachter_cult_broken
Town Guard: Lady Wachter's book club met again last night. Lamps lit in her cellar till dawn. That's a lot of reading.
if not quest.wachter_plot
quest wachter_plot rumored
endif
endif
if not quest.cat_in_the_window
set stella_rumor
quest cat_in_the_window rumored
Town Guard: And there's a girl in a window at Wachterhaus who washes her face with the back of her hand. All day. Two years, and nobody's seen her come out. The Wachters say she's delicate.
elif flag.stella_at_church
Town Guard: Lady Wachter's girl is up at St. Andral's now. Walked out of that house in broad daylight, in her stockings, and spat on the step. Nobody's said a word to her mother. Everybody's said a word to everybody else.
endif
if not quest.the_squire and flag.order_fate != "rest"
Town Guard: The cooper's boy, Cosmin, ran off north a week back with his father's old blanket and a wooden sword. Says he's gone to the dragon's house to join the dead knights. His mother's at the north gate every night with a lamp.
endif
if not quest.one_lantern_too_many and level >= 5
-> vallaki/one_lantern_too_many:guard_news
endif
Town Guard: And the festival, of course. Always the festival.
-> END

~ whos_who
Town Guard: The Baron, Vargas Vallakovich. Festivals, decrees, happiness. Lives in the big house on the square. Izek Strazni's his right hand. Don't shake it; it isn't a hand.
Town Guard: Lady Wachter at Wachterhaus, who the Baron says is plotting, which she probably is. Father Lucian at the church. The Martikovs at the inn. Blinsky the toymaker, who's sad. Henrik the coffin maker, who's busy.
-> END

~ jailer
if flag.vallaki_backed == "baron"
Lockup Warden: Lockup's full of Wachter's hired men. The lady herself is in the stocks, in front of everyone. The Baron visits twice a day to see if she's cheered up.
-> END
elif flag.vallaki_backed == "wachter"
Lockup Warden: The lockup's full of the Baron's sergeants now. Same lockup, same key, different people. I'm still here. Somebody has to hold the key.
-> END
elif flag.vallaki_backed == "neither"
if flag.wachter_fate == "exposed"
Lockup Warden: The council let everyone out. Everyone but her. Lady Wachter's in the back cell with a candle and a book, and she's the calmest prisoner I've ever had. I don't like it.
else
Lockup Warden: The council let everyone out. The lockup's empty. I sit here anyway. It's a good chair.
endif
-> END
endif
Narrator: The lockup is a squat log house with one barred window. Three faces look out of it at you, without much hope.
if flag.malcontents_freed
Lockup Warden: Empty. Somebody let them out. Somebody I'm not going to remember, if anyone asks.
-> END
endif
Lockup Warden: The Baron's malcontents. A cobbler who said it might rain. A widow who laughed at the wrong part of a speech. A boy who drew the Baron. Badly. Until the next festival.
* [Persuasion DC 14] They've done nothing. Let them go home. -> free_ok | free_fail
* [if gold >= 15 and not flag.vallaki_watch_wary] (Press fifteen gold into his hand.) Let them go home. -> free_bribe
* [if gold >= 25 and flag.vallaki_watch_wary] (Press twenty-five gold into his hand.) Let them go home. -> free_bribe_wary
* Goodbye. -> END

~ free_ok
set malcontents_freed
Lockup Warden: Nothing. No. They haven't, have they. Go on, the three of you. Out. If anyone asks, the lock rusted.
Narrator: The cobbler shakes your hand on the way past, very hard, without a word.
approve thistle +2 godrick_pendlebrook +2 wren_featherfoot +2 liriel_dawnsong +1: You talked the Baron's prisoners out of the lockup
-> END

~ free_fail
Lockup Warden: And then I go in the stocks instead, and who lets me out? No. Sorry. Truly.
-> END

~ free_bribe
gold -15
set malcontents_freed
Lockup Warden: Well. That's a sum. That's a rusted lock, that is. Off you go, all three. Quickly.
approve thistle +2 wren_featherfoot +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1 kip_smudgewick +1: You bought the Baron's prisoners out of the lockup
-> END

~ free_bribe_wary
gold -25
set malcontents_freed
Lockup Warden: Twenty-five. The lads at the gate described you, see. Shouting at spears. Being memorable costs extra in this town. Off you go, all three. Quickly.
approve thistle +2 wren_featherfoot +2 godrick_pendlebrook +1 kip_smudgewick +1: You bought the Baron's prisoners out of the lockup
-> END

~ mansion_guard
if flag.vallaki_backed == "wachter"
Town Guard: Lady Wachter receives in the hall now. The Baron's portraits are coming down this afternoon. I'm helping.
-> END
endif
Town Guard: The Baron receives visitors in the great hall. Wipe your boots. Smile on the way in; he notices.
-> END
